WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:14.240
of what we studied in the previous weeks, principally. In the first dialect, the purpose

00:00:14.240 --> 00:00:22.120
was to explain the function of tradition, how you cannot have a culture, a nation, a

00:00:22.120 --> 00:00:28.639
people without a tradition, yes? And therefore, what was the tradition of Israel? In the second

00:00:28.639 --> 00:00:38.840
dialect, he wanted to explain an institution, which was maligned principally by Christianity.

00:00:38.840 --> 00:00:46.520
And this is the rabbinical institution. Until today, there are people who in their mind

00:00:46.520 --> 00:00:53.119
they say, well, Judaism is alright, but look at the rabbis. And when we examine what the

00:00:53.119 --> 00:00:59.680
rabbis were, their function, their obligation, what they accomplished, and this is what

00:00:59.680 --> 00:01:07.160
they did in the second dialect, we see that no other nation in recorded history was as

00:01:07.160 --> 00:01:12.959
fortunate as the people of Israel with having the quality of leadership that we had. And

00:01:12.959 --> 00:01:23.080
that was the second dialect. In this dialect, he wants to analyze not the rabbis as an institution,

00:01:23.080 --> 00:01:32.959
but the actual accomplishments that they made, what they did, yes? And what happened,

00:01:32.959 --> 00:01:39.040
different laws, how to explain those laws, not them, alright, we accept them, we understand

00:01:39.040 --> 00:01:51.599
in general terms, their function, but what is it that they produced? Now, let me begin

00:01:51.599 --> 00:01:59.800
myself with a metaphor that I think would illustrate very clearly the rabbinical institutions.

00:01:59.800 --> 00:02:08.440
On the one hand, we say what the rabbis do is exactly the way that the Torah prescribed.

00:02:08.440 --> 00:02:14.440
But when historians look into things, there is a difference, there are always differences,

00:02:14.440 --> 00:02:22.679
there are differences. So how the rabbis did it, what is it? Now, I have a beautiful

00:02:22.679 --> 00:02:35.279
metaphor. A few, about a hundred and so years ago, there were two brothers, the Wright brothers,

00:02:35.279 --> 00:02:47.240
who discovered the principle of aerodynamics. And they were able to take a monoplane, one

00:02:47.240 --> 00:02:54.559
single engine plane, and I think they were able to fly at something like 25 yards, and

00:02:54.559 --> 00:03:00.520
the altitude was something like, I don't know, 15 or 20 yards, right? They discovered the

00:03:00.520 --> 00:03:10.639
principle of aerodynamics, and they flew for about 25 yards. Now, later on somebody

00:03:10.639 --> 00:03:20.880
says, well, that's good, but instead of flying 25 yards, I want to see if I could fly a thousand

00:03:20.880 --> 00:03:33.279
yards. And at an altitude of, let's say, 100 yards. Now, in order to produce such a

00:03:33.279 --> 00:03:44.039
machine, they had to make some changes. Some changes in the design of the plane. One minute.

00:03:44.039 --> 00:03:50.279
Later on somebody says, well, instead of being a thousand yards, let's see if we can

00:03:50.279 --> 00:04:02.039
make it 50 miles. In order to accomplish this, you have to redesign the airplane. Eventually

00:04:02.039 --> 00:04:11.279
somebody says, I want an airplane that I will be able to cross the Atlantic. Again, engineering

00:04:11.279 --> 00:04:23.679
changes and the Atlantic is crossed. Et cetera, et cetera, et cetera. A jet plane, 747. Some

00:04:23.679 --> 00:04:32.119
interplanetary vehicles that will descend and orbit around within the solar system.

00:04:32.119 --> 00:04:39.279
Now, there's changes, but the changes do not pertain to the law of aerodynamics. It's the

00:04:39.279 --> 00:04:45.239
same law of aerodynamics. There's no change in the law of aerodynamics. But if it's the

00:04:45.239 --> 00:04:49.320
same law of aerodynamics tells me that if the vehicle is going to have such and such

00:04:49.320 --> 00:04:54.160
an engine, well, you need such and such a design in order to be able to accomplish what

00:04:54.160 --> 00:05:01.760
you want. The changes are never, never to the law itself. The law of aerodynamics, nobody

00:05:01.760 --> 00:05:10.200
could change. This is part of the laws of physics. What we could do is change the design

00:05:10.200 --> 00:05:16.399
of our airplanes because what we want today is different than what the Wright brothers

00:05:16.399 --> 00:05:23.600
wanted today. But there is no difference. In a sense, and that's what we're going to

00:05:23.600 --> 00:05:30.480
try to show, and what David Nieto tried to show. He didn't use, obviously, this metaphor,

00:05:30.480 --> 00:05:38.959
this parable, is that the rabbis, the laws of the rabbis, change because the situation

00:05:38.959 --> 00:05:51.559
of the Jew changed. And that situation warranted not a change in the law of the Torah, but

00:05:51.559 --> 00:06:01.079
a redefining of certain niceties. And let me give you an explanation. There is a controversy

00:06:01.079 --> 00:06:07.200
in the Talmud, and I brought this example because he discusses it, and it has been to

00:06:07.200 --> 00:06:12.399
be in the parasha of this week's parasha, Kitabot. It's something very simple. When

00:06:12.399 --> 00:06:18.559
Kitabot El Ha'aretz, when you come to the land of Israel, and you plant it and so on,

00:06:18.559 --> 00:06:25.480
and you have the fruits of your labor, so what you should do? You should take bikurim,

00:06:25.480 --> 00:06:35.000
in Spanish primitivas, the first fruits of the season, you put it in a basket, and you

00:06:35.000 --> 00:06:41.760
bring it to the temple. It's a mitzvah, simple mitzvah. Now there is a controversy in the

00:06:41.760 --> 00:06:47.880
Talmud, and the rabbis elaborate on this. The controversy pertains to the following

00:06:47.880 --> 00:06:59.799
thing. Suppose somebody did not sell his land, but leased his land to somebody. What does

00:06:59.799 --> 00:07:07.959
it mean that I leased my land? The actual real estate belongs to me. But for X amount

00:07:07.959 --> 00:07:19.119
of years, you are permitted to work the land, and whatever you harvest belongs to you. Still

00:07:19.119 --> 00:07:24.959
today, the question of leasing property is part of, say, the American legal system. We

00:07:24.959 --> 00:07:30.559
could lease property. The property, when you lease a property for 90 years or 50 years,

00:07:30.559 --> 00:07:36.000
the property does not belong to you. But during these 50 years or 90 years, you could erect

00:07:36.000 --> 00:07:40.399
a building, a factory, whatever it is. And there is many business reasons why somebody

00:07:40.399 --> 00:07:50.239
would prefer to sell, to lease, rather than to sell. Now, question. Suppose you lease

00:07:50.239 --> 00:07:58.640
the land. Now you harvest the fruit. And now you come to the primitivas, the bikurim, the

00:07:58.640 --> 00:08:06.239
first fruit. Can you take this fruit to the temple? Yes or no? Because when you go to

00:08:06.239 --> 00:08:16.239
the temple, you have to say, thank you to God, and these are the fruits, asenatata li,

00:08:16.239 --> 00:08:26.959
which you gave to me. Now, are these my fruits, that God gave me? When it says God gave me,

00:08:26.959 --> 00:08:38.359
meant the fruit only, or meant the land? Controversy. Now, what is the nature of this

00:08:38.359 --> 00:08:45.359
controversy? Is it that something is wrong with the Torah? Whatever the answer is going

00:08:45.359 --> 00:08:54.960
to be, is it some invention of the rabbis? Or is it that this kind of buying and selling

00:08:54.960 --> 00:09:02.960
emerged at a certain time in history, by the end of the second temple, and therefore,

00:09:02.960 --> 00:09:12.359
the rabbis, they have to meet the new situation. All of a sudden, we buy and sell differently.

00:09:12.359 --> 00:09:20.760
And because we buy and sell differently, we change. We have to know how to apply the law

00:09:20.760 --> 00:09:27.760
of the Torah. Is it that I can say, well, I want an airplane that will be able to carry

00:09:27.760 --> 00:09:33.760
such and such a load, and therefore, I have to figure out, for such and such a load, what

00:09:33.760 --> 00:09:45.359
kind of engine I need to design, etc., etc. So, the principal point of the controversy,

00:09:45.359 --> 00:09:51.960
or the innovations of the rabbis. So, if someone says, well, this is a ridiculous controversy,

00:09:51.960 --> 00:09:59.559
who cares? No, no. The sense is, you gave me. You have to say, you gave me. Is it his

00:09:59.559 --> 00:10:09.659
or not? Do you understand the problem? Let me give you another problem. Also, at the

00:10:09.659 --> 00:10:18.659
end of the second temple, and I want you to see the problems discussed by the rabbis,

00:10:18.659 --> 00:10:30.359
and the nature of these problems. If a person made a vow to bring a korban, a sacrifice,

00:10:30.359 --> 00:10:43.559
to the temple, the first holiday, the first of the three holidays, which are Pesach, Shavuot,

00:10:43.559 --> 00:10:53.159
and Sukkot, he should bring them. If three holidays pass, and he didn't bring them, he

00:10:53.159 --> 00:11:08.159
made a sin, Balti Ahir. Now, problem in the Talmud. What happens if a person dies? He

00:11:08.159 --> 00:11:17.159
made such and such, this sheep, goat, whatever it is, is going to be a korban for the temple.

00:11:17.159 --> 00:11:30.159
If the person dies, his children inherit his property. Do the children have the obligation to bring

00:11:30.159 --> 00:11:40.159
this animal to the temple? And suppose they did not bring the animal to the temple, and three

00:11:40.159 --> 00:11:51.159
holidays elapsed. Are they committing a sin? Discussion with the rabbis, rabbinical institutions.

00:11:51.159 --> 00:11:58.159
What happened? What happened is something that didn't happen before to us. At the end of the

00:11:58.159 --> 00:12:06.159
second temple, hundreds of thousands of Jews were killed, were massacred. And therefore,

00:12:06.159 --> 00:12:23.159
this problem became a burning problem. What to do? So, as new situations, as our socio-political

00:12:23.159 --> 00:12:38.159
economic situation changed abruptly, new problems came about. And when those problems came about,

00:12:38.159 --> 00:12:51.159
the rabbis had to give solutions. Now, a principle which is fundamental. There are controversies

00:12:51.159 --> 00:12:58.159
among the rabbis. And I want to see what brought about these controversies. But following and

00:12:58.159 --> 00:13:08.159
citing my manners, Rabbi David Nieto says, every controversy that we had in the Talmud pertained

00:13:08.159 --> 00:13:20.159
not to the substance, to the akkar, the principle of the law, but only to details. Details. Details

00:13:20.159 --> 00:13:33.159
that arouse because new circumstances arouse. Example, now we lease land. It's a new situation.

00:13:34.159 --> 00:13:42.159
We know the law, what the law says. The law says only the proprietor may come and bring bikkurim.

00:13:42.159 --> 00:13:47.159
But we do not know whether the proprietor means the proprietor of the fruits or the proprietor of the

00:13:47.159 --> 00:13:56.159
real estate. We know that the baal, the owner, the proprietor of the korban has to bring it to the

00:13:56.159 --> 00:14:03.159
temple. We know that the proprietor, if he doesn't bring it, makes a sin. But now the children are the

00:14:03.159 --> 00:14:14.159
proprietor. Do they make a sin or not? The controversies of the rabbis pertain only to the details.

00:14:14.159 --> 00:14:20.159
Let me give you another example. We all say Shema Yisrael Adonai Eloheinu Adonai Echad.

00:14:22.159 --> 00:14:28.159
Now, and this I'm going to explain. How do we say the Shema?

00:14:29.159 --> 00:14:40.159
Bet Shammai, another rabbi, Rabbi Tafon says, it's written Beshochvecha Uvkumecha.

00:14:40.159 --> 00:14:50.159
Beshochvecha means when you're about to sleep and when you get up. And they say, you know what it means?

00:14:50.159 --> 00:15:03.159
That at night you have to sit down when you say the Shema. And in the morning, Uvkumecha, you say the Shema standing up.

00:15:03.159 --> 00:15:17.159
Beshochvecha Uvkumecha. Kams Bet Hillel, say no no no no. Beshochvecha means at the time that you're going to go to sleep.

00:15:18.159 --> 00:15:27.159
Uvkumecha means at the time that you get up in the morning. Now pay attention.

00:15:27.159 --> 00:15:42.159
The controversy does not pertain to the substance of the law. Namely, every male Jew must recite Keriash Shema once in the morning and once at night.

00:15:42.159 --> 00:15:54.159
There are no controversies pertaining to the substance of the law. The controversies that you find in the Talmud apply to details.

00:15:54.159 --> 00:16:12.159
What it calls Seifim, secondary circumstances of the law. Now, why there were controversies? Why happened?

00:16:12.159 --> 00:16:27.159
Very important thing. We Jews, much before the Romans, much before the United States of America, we had a judicial system.

00:16:28.159 --> 00:16:46.159
And people forget that we had also a system whereby you could appeal a law. Namely we had, principally we had three kinds of courts.

00:16:46.159 --> 00:17:13.160
I want you to remember this. You had a court of three judges. And this court cannot deal with criminal law, only with business law, with monetary law, but not with criminal law.

00:17:13.160 --> 00:17:26.160
If I hit somebody, which is a crime in Jewish areas, if I kill somebody, anything that would involve a crime, this court of three cannot deal with it.

00:17:26.160 --> 00:17:49.160
So you had one court of three. Then you had courts of 23 members. And this court could deal with criminal matters, and if needed be, they could even apply capital punishment.

00:17:49.160 --> 00:18:11.160
And then, there was the Beddin, the Sanhedrin, which was set at the Beit HaMikdash, had 71 members, and it dealt not only with criminal law, but political law.

00:18:11.160 --> 00:18:28.160
They could even summon the king, and trial the king. In the Jewish system, the king is subject to the law. The supreme court can summon a king.

00:18:28.160 --> 00:18:55.160
Now, up to the destruction of the Temple, there were no controversies among the Jewish people. Why? Whenever there was a controversy among the different courts, throughout Israel, throughout the Jewish diaspora, the matter would be appealed, and it would go to the court of 23.

00:18:55.160 --> 00:19:12.160
If there was a dispute among the courts of 23, you further appeal this matter, and you bring it to the supreme court. And the supreme court will give a final decision.

00:19:12.160 --> 00:19:28.160
And that would be the law. With the destruction of the Temple, we no longer had a supreme court. Now, suppose there is a Beddin in Tiberia.

00:19:28.160 --> 00:19:44.160
It says, this is permitted. When you have a Beddin in Caesarea, or in Babel, that says something different.

00:19:44.160 --> 00:20:07.160
You have no legal means to summon the parties, and to force them to come to an agreement. So one says, mutar, permissible.

00:20:07.160 --> 00:20:33.160
The other says, what? It's forbidden. And because we did not have a central authority, a central judicial authority, there was no means by which to determine what the law is.

00:20:34.160 --> 00:20:55.160
And because the sages said, there were students who misunderstood the teachers, because the teachers used different words, and they thought that the respective teachers were in disagreement with each other.

00:20:55.160 --> 00:21:24.160
And because of this, there was a lot of controversy among the Jewish people. Imagine America, United States of America, without a supreme court, how many minutes, hours, days, maybe weeks would pass before there would break civil war between the states?

00:21:25.160 --> 00:21:49.160
The miracle that happened, is that in spite of the controversy, without a central force, with authority to say to the courts, come before us, present your case, and we'll decide.

00:21:50.160 --> 00:22:05.160
Still, the Jewish people were able to solve the situations, and to minimize the controversies.

00:22:05.160 --> 00:22:26.160
Now, I will explain more, but before, let me tell you something that he asked. He said, well, something is strange among the Jewish people. We always say that those rabbis that were before us, they have more authority than we do.

00:22:27.160 --> 00:22:43.160
Well, why? We see that throughout our history, throughout history, the later authorities know more than the preceding authorities.

00:22:43.160 --> 00:23:00.160
And he brings as an example, the great, great progress made in science in the 17th century, where I was living, in the field of astronomy, in the field of medicine.

00:23:00.160 --> 00:23:19.160
So he says, how could you say that the preceding rabbis knew more than us today, when we see that the whole world is always, the newer generation knows more than the preceding generation.

00:23:20.160 --> 00:23:32.160
Do you understand the question he's asking? He says, we should be able to solve the problems that the hachamim in Talmud says, because we are more intelligent, we know more. There is a progress in the development of the human brain.

00:23:33.160 --> 00:23:41.160
So you're going to tell me that we are like angels, and we are just like coming human beings, because we see that this is not a fact.

00:23:42.160 --> 00:23:58.160
How to answer this question? Now he gives an answer, and I'll be frank with you. I would not have been able to understand that answer, would not be because of the fact that I read another book.

00:23:59.160 --> 00:24:07.160
And through the other book, which I'll tell you in a minute about it, I was able to understand what Rabbi David Nieto was talking all about.

00:24:08.160 --> 00:24:20.160
He says, Rabbi Nieto is, no, we are more intelligent than the preceding one. Modern man sees, understands things that the ancients were incapable of doing.

00:24:21.160 --> 00:24:30.160
Imagine I would tell to somebody eight years ago about that space and time are relative. The person will not be able to understand.

00:24:31.160 --> 00:24:37.160
The simple notion of what a college boy knows today through Einstein, that relativity of time and space.

00:24:38.160 --> 00:24:43.160
They would not be able, just to understand the concept, let alone their mathematics, they would not be able to understand it.

00:24:44.160 --> 00:24:52.160
Or a person in the 16th century could not understand calculus, it would not be possible, the brain could not grasp calculus, it would be impossible.

00:24:53.160 --> 00:25:01.160
And today, as we progress, we see that the human brain is developing a fantastic space.

00:25:02.160 --> 00:25:08.160
Now he says, give this following answer, and I will try to explain it to you.

00:25:09.160 --> 00:25:21.160
He says, the reason that we don't know Torah as much as the preceding ones, is not because we are less intelligent, but because we are in Galut.

00:25:22.160 --> 00:25:33.160
Because we are in Galut, we know mathematics more than biology, I don't know, microphysics, everything is there.

00:25:34.160 --> 00:25:36.160
But Torah we cannot know because we are in Galut.

00:25:37.160 --> 00:25:39.160
What does it mean?

00:25:40.160 --> 00:25:48.160
Again, Rabbi David Nieto is very dear to me, and I have been very comfortable with him for many years.

00:25:49.160 --> 00:25:57.160
There is another Rabbi, I am sure that you have your favorite, I don't know, musicians or philosophers or playwriters.

00:25:58.160 --> 00:26:02.160
So I have my favorite hachamim, I have a specialist.

00:26:03.160 --> 00:26:08.160
And one of them is called Rabbi Yosef Ya'aves Hechasid.

00:26:09.160 --> 00:26:15.160
He was one of the Jews who left not Spain, but Portugal.

00:26:15.160 --> 00:26:17.160
He was from Galut, Portugal.

00:26:18.160 --> 00:26:24.160
And he left Portugal around 1507, right at the beginning of the 1500s.

00:26:25.160 --> 00:26:31.160
Now, he was an extraordinary man, he is called Hachasid because he was such a devout and pious man.

00:26:32.160 --> 00:26:34.160
And he wrote innumerable kinds of books.

00:26:35.160 --> 00:26:39.160
And above all, when he reached Thessaloniki, he established a printing press.

00:26:40.160 --> 00:26:43.160
I think he belonged to a wealthy family.

00:26:44.160 --> 00:26:50.160
And many, many books printed in Thessaloniki came out from the house of Rabbi Yosef Ya'aves.

00:26:51.160 --> 00:26:57.160
Eventually, the family moved to Egypt, and I know one of the descendants,

00:26:58.160 --> 00:27:05.160
who was one of the great poets of our time, he just died a few years ago, Edmond Javez.

00:27:06.160 --> 00:27:11.160
One of the great poets, somebody wrote in France that there is no other poet in France

00:27:12.160 --> 00:27:14.160
who was not directly influenced by the poetry of Edmond Javez.

00:27:15.160 --> 00:27:17.160
A very good Jew, and he passed away.

00:27:18.160 --> 00:27:21.160
So, his ancestor, Rabbi Yosef, says like this.

00:27:22.160 --> 00:27:26.160
Once, he was summoned by the king of Portugal.

00:27:27.160 --> 00:27:33.160
And he says to the king in Portugal, I want to ask you a question.

00:27:34.160 --> 00:27:39.160
How do you say that when the Mashiach will come,

00:27:40.160 --> 00:27:46.160
you will be able to be the most powerful kingdom on earth?

00:27:47.160 --> 00:27:50.160
When I see you, you are the drag of everybody.

00:27:51.160 --> 00:27:52.160
You are the lowest of the lowest.

00:27:53.160 --> 00:27:54.160
How can you do that? How could you say that?

00:27:55.160 --> 00:27:58.160
Rabbi Yosef Ya'aves writes that at the time he didn't know the answer,

00:27:59.160 --> 00:28:00.160
he didn't have the final answer, he didn't know what to answer.

00:28:00.160 --> 00:28:03.160
And as they were asking him the question,

00:28:04.160 --> 00:28:08.160
the slaves, the servants of the king, they come,

00:28:09.160 --> 00:28:17.160
and they announced to him that once they had captured two cubs, two lion cubs,

00:28:18.160 --> 00:28:20.160
so wild lions, you know, not real lions,

00:28:21.160 --> 00:28:25.160
something like the jaguars, those wild cats in Europe.

00:28:26.160 --> 00:28:32.160
And they had captured two wild baby cubs,

00:28:33.160 --> 00:28:35.160
they put the color to each of them,

00:28:36.160 --> 00:28:39.160
and they raised them for about, I don't know, a year or so on.

00:28:40.160 --> 00:28:44.160
And then one of them managed to escape.

00:28:45.160 --> 00:28:50.160
And at the moment that the king was asking the question to Rabbi Yosef Ya'aves,

00:28:50.160 --> 00:28:56.160
Rabbi Yosef Ya'aves, his slaves told him that they recaptured after X amount of years,

00:28:57.160 --> 00:28:59.160
the brother.

00:29:00.160 --> 00:29:09.160
When they captured, the king and everybody else saw that this brother was much larger,

00:29:09.160 --> 00:29:21.160
had more courage, stronger, wilder than his brother.

00:29:22.160 --> 00:29:27.160
And Rabbi Yosef Ya'aves caught the thing on the spot,

00:29:28.160 --> 00:29:33.160
and he says, my lord, how could you explain two twin brothers,

00:29:33.160 --> 00:29:40.160
two twin brothers, one seems so shy and so weak and so passive,

00:29:41.160 --> 00:29:48.160
and the other so strong, so virile, what's the meaning?

00:29:49.160 --> 00:29:52.160
And the king says, no problem,

00:29:53.160 --> 00:29:57.160
because this second one, he lived in the wilderness,

00:29:58.160 --> 00:30:03.160
natural habitat, and therefore was able to develop.

00:30:04.160 --> 00:30:06.160
Whereas this is a prisoner.

00:30:07.160 --> 00:30:10.160
He says, king, this is our answer.

00:30:11.160 --> 00:30:15.160
You see us now at the bottom of society,

00:30:16.160 --> 00:30:19.160
because we are in prison.

00:30:21.160 --> 00:30:25.160
But when we are going to break out of prison,

00:30:26.160 --> 00:30:32.160
and to roam through our natural habitat,

00:30:33.160 --> 00:30:36.160
we are not going to be like we are now.

00:30:37.160 --> 00:30:40.160
We are going to fully develop,

00:30:41.160 --> 00:30:48.160
and then, yes, we will be the most powerful nation on earth.

00:30:49.160 --> 00:30:53.160
Because of this story, I understood, Rabbi,

00:30:54.160 --> 00:30:56.160
David Nieto,

00:30:57.160 --> 00:31:00.160
we could be intelligent in every single facet in the world,

00:31:01.160 --> 00:31:07.160
but as long as we are not growing in a natural Jewish habitat,

00:31:09.160 --> 00:31:19.160
our Jewish mind will be unable to develop fully.

00:31:20.160 --> 00:31:24.160
And therefore, and therefore,

00:31:25.160 --> 00:31:31.160
we are inferior to the early hachavim.

00:31:32.160 --> 00:31:35.160
Not because we are genetically stupid,

00:31:36.160 --> 00:31:43.160
but because we did not have the opportunity to grow in a Jewish milieu.

00:31:44.160 --> 00:31:47.160
We are not growing in a Jewish habitat.

00:31:48.160 --> 00:31:51.160
And until this happens,

00:31:52.160 --> 00:31:56.160
our understanding of the Torah is less than perfect.

00:31:57.160 --> 00:32:00.160
This is the answer of Rabbi David Nieto.

00:32:01.160 --> 00:32:02.160
Fantastic, brilliant.

00:32:03.160 --> 00:32:07.160
Now, how then we come to come to decisions?

00:32:08.160 --> 00:32:10.160
How are we going to become Maharaka?

00:32:11.160 --> 00:32:12.160
No problem.

00:32:13.160 --> 00:32:17.160
And he brings a metaphor

00:32:18.160 --> 00:32:22.160
that was introduced in Jewish literature

00:32:23.160 --> 00:32:26.160
by one of the exiles from Spain in 1492.

00:32:27.160 --> 00:32:30.160
And there was another gentleman, I love him,

00:32:31.160 --> 00:32:33.160
that he took it from the Jews.

00:32:34.160 --> 00:32:37.160
Isaac Newton takes the same metaphor.

00:32:38.160 --> 00:32:43.160
Rabbi Yishak de Leon, left Spain in 1492,

00:32:44.160 --> 00:32:45.160
writes a book.

00:32:46.160 --> 00:32:50.160
There is a controversy between Haramban Maimonides

00:32:51.160 --> 00:32:54.160
and Haramban Nachmanides

00:32:55.160 --> 00:32:57.160
about how to count the 630 mitzvot.

00:32:58.160 --> 00:32:59.160
A controversy.

00:33:00.160 --> 00:33:02.160
Now, he writes a book.

00:33:02.160 --> 00:33:03.160
He says,

00:33:04.160 --> 00:33:07.160
I am going to show who is right and who is wrong.

00:33:08.160 --> 00:33:10.160
He says, who am I?

00:33:12.160 --> 00:33:14.160
How could I say,

00:33:15.160 --> 00:33:17.160
this point Haramban is right, this point Haramban is right.

00:33:18.160 --> 00:33:20.160
Who am I? How could I say such a thing?

00:33:22.160 --> 00:33:24.160
So he invented

00:33:25.160 --> 00:33:28.160
a beautiful metaphor, which I believe in it.

00:33:28.160 --> 00:33:30.160
This is absolutely benevolent.

00:33:31.160 --> 00:33:33.160
He says, by nature,

00:33:36.160 --> 00:33:38.160
the sight of a giant,

00:33:39.160 --> 00:33:40.160
what a giant sees,

00:33:41.160 --> 00:33:42.160
because he is taller,

00:33:43.160 --> 00:33:46.160
he has a bigger command in sight

00:33:47.160 --> 00:33:49.160
than a dwarf.

00:33:51.160 --> 00:33:54.160
The dwarf simply cannot see

00:33:55.160 --> 00:33:57.160
as long and as far

00:33:58.160 --> 00:34:00.160
as a giant.

00:34:01.160 --> 00:34:02.160
But there is a trick, he says.

00:34:03.160 --> 00:34:04.160
The trick is,

00:34:05.160 --> 00:34:07.160
if this dwarf

00:34:08.159 --> 00:34:10.159
manages to climb

00:34:11.159 --> 00:34:13.159
on the shoulders of giant,

00:34:15.159 --> 00:34:18.159
he will be able to see farther

00:34:19.159 --> 00:34:20.159
than the giant.

00:34:21.159 --> 00:34:23.159
Now he says, Rabbi Yishak de Leon,

00:34:24.159 --> 00:34:26.159
says, I am a dwarf.

00:34:27.159 --> 00:34:30.159
Haramban, the Ramban, are giants.

00:34:31.159 --> 00:34:33.159
But what I am going to do is, I am going to climb on their shoulders.

00:34:34.159 --> 00:34:37.159
And this, what the Rabbi David Neto says,

00:34:38.159 --> 00:34:40.159
the early Rabbis

00:34:41.159 --> 00:34:42.159
were greater than us.

00:34:43.159 --> 00:34:44.159
However,

00:34:47.159 --> 00:34:49.159
if we, when we come and study Halacha,

00:34:50.159 --> 00:34:51.159
that's the way it should be,

00:34:52.159 --> 00:34:53.159
we study all the Hachamim,

00:34:53.159 --> 00:34:56.159
we understand their ideas,

00:34:57.159 --> 00:34:59.159
in other words,

00:35:00.159 --> 00:35:02.159
we climb on their shoulders,

00:35:03.159 --> 00:35:06.159
we could see even farther.

00:35:07.159 --> 00:35:09.159
We are the dwarfs,

00:35:10.159 --> 00:35:14.159
standing on the shoulders of giants.

00:35:15.159 --> 00:35:16.159
And that is the methodology

00:35:17.159 --> 00:35:19.159
that traditional Hachamim adopt.

00:35:20.159 --> 00:35:22.159
When they ask us a question about Halacha,

00:35:23.159 --> 00:35:27.159
I don't say the first thing that pops in my mind.

00:35:28.159 --> 00:35:29.159
What I have to do

00:35:30.159 --> 00:35:32.159
is to make a total research

00:35:33.159 --> 00:35:35.159
of the whole history,

00:35:36.159 --> 00:35:38.159
whatever the Hachamim said throughout the times.

00:35:39.159 --> 00:35:42.159
And then, I learn from them,

00:35:43.159 --> 00:35:44.159
and there is a word that I like very much,

00:35:45.159 --> 00:35:46.159
I use the word, the term,

00:35:47.159 --> 00:35:48.159
the accumulation of knowledge.

00:35:49.159 --> 00:35:50.159
Yes?

00:35:50.159 --> 00:35:53.159
And then, one step higher,

00:35:54.159 --> 00:35:55.159
and we try to climb on their shoulders,

00:35:56.159 --> 00:35:57.159
and to say,

00:35:58.159 --> 00:36:00.159
as far as I can see, thanks to them,

00:36:01.159 --> 00:36:02.159
and we make the Pesach Halacha.

00:36:03.159 --> 00:36:05.159
You know, we tremble in fear.

00:36:06.159 --> 00:36:07.159
Yes?

00:36:08.159 --> 00:36:09.159
But because we are standing on their shoulders,

00:36:10.159 --> 00:36:11.159
we feel that, we feel comfortable,

00:36:12.159 --> 00:36:13.159
a little bit less, less panic.

00:36:14.159 --> 00:36:15.159
Alright?

00:36:16.159 --> 00:36:18.159
So here, we have a very interesting

00:36:18.159 --> 00:36:21.159
concept

00:36:22.159 --> 00:36:24.159
of what Hachamim are,

00:36:25.159 --> 00:36:26.159
what they were,

00:36:27.159 --> 00:36:28.159
and

00:36:29.159 --> 00:36:30.159
our present role

00:36:31.159 --> 00:36:33.159
in relation to this chain

00:36:34.159 --> 00:36:35.159
of tradition.

00:36:36.159 --> 00:36:38.159
Now, that's why he says that,

00:36:39.159 --> 00:36:40.159
he uses a fantastic word,

00:36:41.159 --> 00:36:42.159
he says, los modernos, the modern, means us.

00:36:43.159 --> 00:36:44.159
Yes?

00:36:44.159 --> 00:36:46.159
Los antiguos penetran menos que los antiguos.

00:36:47.159 --> 00:36:48.159
But, now you understand why,

00:36:49.159 --> 00:36:50.159
the impossibility to understand Torah,

00:36:51.159 --> 00:36:52.159
unless we are in

00:36:53.159 --> 00:36:55.159
an un-Galut atmosphere,

00:36:56.159 --> 00:36:57.159
and the necessity to

00:36:58.159 --> 00:36:59.159
climb over their shoulders,

00:37:00.159 --> 00:37:01.159
to be able to understand

00:37:02.159 --> 00:37:03.159
the meaning of the Torah.

00:37:04.159 --> 00:37:05.159
Now,

00:37:06.159 --> 00:37:08.159
he asks another question.

00:37:11.159 --> 00:37:13.159
There are many misthoughts.

00:37:14.159 --> 00:37:16.159
That were instituted by Hachamim.

00:37:17.159 --> 00:37:19.159
For good reasons.

00:37:20.159 --> 00:37:21.159
But they were instituted by Hachamim.

00:37:22.159 --> 00:37:24.159
Netilat Elayim,

00:37:25.159 --> 00:37:26.159
and let me explain to you

00:37:27.159 --> 00:37:28.159
what Netilat Elayim is all about.

00:37:29.159 --> 00:37:30.159
Netilat Elayim has nothing to do with hygiene.

00:37:31.159 --> 00:37:32.159
Nothing to do.

00:37:33.159 --> 00:37:35.159
As a matter of fact, if your hands are filthy,

00:37:36.159 --> 00:37:37.159
for whatever reason,

00:37:38.159 --> 00:37:39.159
I mean, you were painting the house,

00:37:40.159 --> 00:37:41.159
now you have painted over this,

00:37:42.159 --> 00:37:43.159
you cannot make Netilat Elayim

00:37:44.159 --> 00:37:45.159
if your hands are not washed,

00:37:46.159 --> 00:37:47.159
and you made Netilat Elayim,

00:37:48.159 --> 00:37:49.159
Netilat Elayim is not good.

00:37:50.159 --> 00:37:51.159
Yes.

00:37:52.159 --> 00:37:53.159
What is Netilat Elayim?

00:37:54.159 --> 00:37:55.159
Let me explain you.

00:37:56.159 --> 00:37:57.159
At the temple,

00:37:59.159 --> 00:38:01.159
when the priest ate the Korban,

00:38:03.159 --> 00:38:04.159
they had to wash their hands.

00:38:05.159 --> 00:38:06.159
That's written in the Torah.

00:38:07.159 --> 00:38:09.159
There was a kior, a special container,

00:38:10.159 --> 00:38:12.159
built first by Moses,

00:38:12.159 --> 00:38:14.159
and then later on the first temple by King Solomon,

00:38:15.159 --> 00:38:18.159
and they were washing their hands.

00:38:19.159 --> 00:38:21.159
If they ate Terumah,

00:38:22.159 --> 00:38:25.159
what the Israelites gave them,

00:38:26.159 --> 00:38:28.159
the sort of taxes for the Kwanim,

00:38:29.159 --> 00:38:30.159
also Netilat Elayim.

00:38:31.159 --> 00:38:32.159
If we Israelites,

00:38:33.159 --> 00:38:34.159
we ate something from the temple,

00:38:35.159 --> 00:38:36.159
Korban,

00:38:37.159 --> 00:38:39.159
that's to make Netilat Elayim also.

00:38:39.159 --> 00:38:41.159
If we ate Maaser,

00:38:42.159 --> 00:38:43.159
the Jishmah,

00:38:44.159 --> 00:38:46.159
the Jishmah was permitted to eat Maaser.

00:38:47.159 --> 00:38:49.159
Levin says it's permitted to eat Maaser.

00:38:50.159 --> 00:38:51.159
We had to make Netilat Elayim.

00:38:53.159 --> 00:38:55.159
The temple was destroyed.

00:38:57.159 --> 00:38:59.159
No more Netilat Elayim,

00:39:00.159 --> 00:39:02.159
no more eating from the temple.

00:39:04.159 --> 00:39:06.159
The priests were absolute genius.

00:39:07.159 --> 00:39:09.159
The priests were absolute genius.

00:39:10.159 --> 00:39:12.159
In the postulated principle, more or less,

00:39:14.159 --> 00:39:19.159
you could take the Jew out of the temple,

00:39:20.159 --> 00:39:22.159
but you cannot take the temple out of the Jew.

00:39:23.159 --> 00:39:25.159
When we're going to eat bread,

00:39:27.159 --> 00:39:29.159
we're going to make Netilat Elayim,

00:39:31.159 --> 00:39:32.159
because our food

00:39:33.159 --> 00:39:35.159
is as if it is coming

00:39:36.159 --> 00:39:38.159
from the Mizveah, from the altar of the Almighty God.

00:39:41.159 --> 00:39:42.159
The altar of God

00:39:43.159 --> 00:39:46.159
is not only that place in Yerushalayim,

00:39:47.159 --> 00:39:48.159
and of course if you take from the altar,

00:39:49.159 --> 00:39:50.159
or directly from the temple,

00:39:50.159 --> 00:39:51.159
like Maaser,

00:39:52.159 --> 00:39:53.159
or Bikurim,

00:39:53.159 --> 00:39:54.159
you have to make Netilat Elayim.

00:39:55.159 --> 00:39:58.159
Well, well, well, the temple is,

00:39:59.159 --> 00:40:01.159
the edifice is gone,

00:40:02.159 --> 00:40:03.159
but when we work,

00:40:04.159 --> 00:40:05.159
and we toil,

00:40:06.159 --> 00:40:09.159
and we take a few pennies and buy a loaf of bread,

00:40:10.159 --> 00:40:11.159
this loaf of bread

00:40:12.159 --> 00:40:13.159
comes also from the Mizveah of God.

00:40:14.159 --> 00:40:16.159
And therefore we make Netilat Elayim.

00:40:17.159 --> 00:40:18.159
Simple idea.

00:40:19.159 --> 00:40:20.159
As if we were in the temple.

00:40:21.159 --> 00:40:22.159
Zeya Mizveah.

00:40:24.159 --> 00:40:25.159
Hashem if you don't know,

00:40:25.159 --> 00:40:26.159
that's what we say,

00:40:26.159 --> 00:40:27.159
many Jews,

00:40:27.159 --> 00:40:28.159
they have the custom,

00:40:28.159 --> 00:40:29.159
when they have the table,

00:40:29.159 --> 00:40:30.159
they say Zeya Mizveah.

00:40:30.159 --> 00:40:31.159
This is the altar of the Almighty God.

00:40:31.159 --> 00:40:32.159
I'm eating like this.

00:40:32.159 --> 00:40:33.159
That's why we put salt,

00:40:36.159 --> 00:40:37.159
that's custom,

00:40:37.159 --> 00:40:38.159
it's not obligation.

00:40:38.159 --> 00:40:39.159
Because,

00:40:40.159 --> 00:40:41.159
the Korban,

00:40:41.159 --> 00:40:42.159
at the Mizveah,

00:40:43.159 --> 00:40:44.159
it was always with salt.

00:40:45.159 --> 00:40:46.159
Fine.

00:40:47.159 --> 00:40:49.159
We have other Mizvot like this,

00:40:50.159 --> 00:40:51.159
instituted by rabbis.

00:40:53.159 --> 00:40:54.159
The question is,

00:40:56.159 --> 00:40:57.159
how can we say,

00:40:58.159 --> 00:40:59.159
but it seems to be a lie.

00:41:01.159 --> 00:41:02.159
In the Berachah we say,

00:41:02.159 --> 00:41:05.159
Asher kideshanu b'mizvotah vesivanu,

00:41:06.159 --> 00:41:08.159
al Netilat Elayim.

00:41:09.159 --> 00:41:10.159
Blessed are you the Lord,

00:41:11.159 --> 00:41:14.159
because you have commanded us,

00:41:17.159 --> 00:41:18.159
to make Netilat Elayim.

00:41:19.159 --> 00:41:20.159
Sorry, it's a lie.

00:41:21.159 --> 00:41:22.159
It's a lie.

00:41:23.159 --> 00:41:24.159
In no place you open the Chumash,

00:41:24.159 --> 00:41:25.159
in no place...

00:41:32.159 --> 00:41:33.159
How can we come to say,

00:41:34.159 --> 00:41:35.159
Asher kideshanu b'mizvotah vesivanu,

00:41:36.159 --> 00:41:37.159
al Netilat Elayim?

00:41:38.159 --> 00:41:39.159
It's a lie.

00:41:40.159 --> 00:41:41.159
It's a lie.

00:41:42.159 --> 00:41:43.159
It's a lie.

00:41:44.159 --> 00:41:45.159
It's a lie.

00:41:46.159 --> 00:41:47.159
It's a lie.

00:41:48.159 --> 00:41:49.159
It's a lie.

00:41:50.159 --> 00:41:51.159
It's a lie.

00:41:52.159 --> 00:41:53.159
It's a lie.

00:41:54.159 --> 00:41:55.159
It's a lie.

00:41:56.159 --> 00:41:57.159
It's a lie.

00:41:58.159 --> 00:41:59.159
It's a lie.

00:42:00.159 --> 00:42:01.159
It's a lie.

00:42:02.159 --> 00:42:03.159
Where is it written?

00:42:03.159 --> 00:42:04.159
No place is written.

00:42:05.159 --> 00:42:07.159
Here comes another principle,

00:42:08.159 --> 00:42:10.159
about the Rabbinic institution.

00:42:12.159 --> 00:42:13.159
The Torah says,

00:42:14.159 --> 00:42:15.159
that whenever we have problems,

00:42:16.159 --> 00:42:18.159
whenever we have questions,

00:42:19.159 --> 00:42:20.159
conflicts,

00:42:21.159 --> 00:42:22.159
Vekamta vealita,

00:42:23.159 --> 00:42:25.159
El hamakom asher yuvchar Adonai Elohecha.

00:42:26.159 --> 00:42:27.159
And then it says,

00:42:28.159 --> 00:42:29.159
Veasita,

00:42:29.159 --> 00:42:31.159
Al pii hatora asherucha.

00:42:32.159 --> 00:42:34.159
Lo tasum minadaba sheyagidu lecha,

00:42:35.159 --> 00:42:37.159
Yamin usmon.

00:42:38.159 --> 00:42:41.159
The Torah, the Almighty Lord told us,

00:42:43.159 --> 00:42:45.159
whenever we have problems, questions,

00:42:46.159 --> 00:42:47.159
conflicts,

00:42:48.159 --> 00:42:49.159
we should go to the Rabbis,

00:42:50.159 --> 00:42:51.159
listen to this,

00:42:52.159 --> 00:42:53.159
and Veasita,

00:42:54.159 --> 00:42:55.159
and you should follow,

00:42:56.159 --> 00:42:58.159
Al pii hatora asherucha.

00:42:59.159 --> 00:43:00.159
The Lord, they tell you.

00:43:02.159 --> 00:43:03.159
So here comes a point,

00:43:04.159 --> 00:43:06.159
that first was defended by my managers,

00:43:07.159 --> 00:43:08.159
and,

00:43:09.159 --> 00:43:10.159
eventually by Rabbi Davinieto,

00:43:11.159 --> 00:43:13.159
saying to you in effect,

00:43:14.159 --> 00:43:15.159
that if you obey,

00:43:16.159 --> 00:43:17.159
if you follow,

00:43:18.159 --> 00:43:19.159
if you listen,

00:43:21.159 --> 00:43:22.159
to Amisva,

00:43:23.159 --> 00:43:24.159
to a commandment,

00:43:25.159 --> 00:43:26.159
Rabbinic, by the Rabbis,

00:43:27.159 --> 00:43:28.159
in point of fact,

00:43:29.159 --> 00:43:30.159
you are listening to the Torah.

00:43:31.159 --> 00:43:32.159
Because you listen to the Rabbis,

00:43:33.159 --> 00:43:34.159
not because of the Rabbis,

00:43:37.159 --> 00:43:38.159
you're listening to the Rabbis,

00:43:39.159 --> 00:43:40.159
because God told you to listen to them.

00:43:42.159 --> 00:43:43.159
It is explicit in the Torah.

00:43:46.159 --> 00:43:47.159
It's just like when I,

00:43:48.159 --> 00:43:49.159
comes a police officer,

00:43:51.159 --> 00:43:52.159
and tell me,

00:43:53.159 --> 00:43:54.159
Stop!

00:43:55.159 --> 00:43:57.159
I don't care about him.

00:43:58.159 --> 00:44:00.159
I'm not stopping because he tells me stop.

00:44:02.159 --> 00:44:04.159
I am stopping because he's an agent

00:44:06.159 --> 00:44:07.159
of the state,

00:44:09.159 --> 00:44:10.159
or the federal government,

00:44:12.159 --> 00:44:13.159
or another

00:44:14.159 --> 00:44:15.159
government institution,

00:44:16.159 --> 00:44:18.159
and if I disobey him,

00:44:19.159 --> 00:44:20.159
I'm not disobeying

00:44:21.159 --> 00:44:23.159
Mr. A or Mr. B or Mr. C,

00:44:24.159 --> 00:44:25.159
I am disobeying

00:44:26.159 --> 00:44:27.159
the state of Florida,

00:44:28.159 --> 00:44:29.159
or maybe the federal government.

00:44:31.159 --> 00:44:32.159
The hachamim

00:44:35.159 --> 00:44:37.159
are the agents appointed by God.

00:44:38.159 --> 00:44:39.159
And therefore,

00:44:39.159 --> 00:44:41.159
Asher kideshanu b'mitzvotav v'sibanu,

00:44:42.159 --> 00:44:43.159
a'an letilat yadayim,

00:44:44.159 --> 00:44:45.159
lehad likneshe Shabbat,

00:44:46.159 --> 00:44:47.159
the light of Shabbat is written

00:44:48.159 --> 00:44:49.159
no place in the Torah is written

00:44:50.159 --> 00:44:52.159
you light candles for Shabbat.

00:44:52.159 --> 00:44:53.159
That's not written.

00:44:54.159 --> 00:44:56.159
The one who is a berachah,

00:44:57.159 --> 00:44:58.159
because,

00:44:59.159 --> 00:45:00.159
and this is unanimous

00:45:01.159 --> 00:45:02.159
among the Jewish people,

00:45:05.159 --> 00:45:06.159
to obey

00:45:07.159 --> 00:45:09.159
to a rabbinic institution,

00:45:10.159 --> 00:45:11.159
is to obey

00:45:12.159 --> 00:45:13.159
the word of God,

00:45:14.159 --> 00:45:15.159
because God

00:45:15.159 --> 00:45:16.159
told us,

00:45:18.159 --> 00:45:20.159
These are my agents.

00:45:20.159 --> 00:45:22.159
These are my agents.

00:45:24.159 --> 00:45:26.159
That's a very important idea.

00:45:27.159 --> 00:45:29.159
But I want to further develop

00:45:31.159 --> 00:45:33.159
some of the things that the rabbis did

00:45:35.159 --> 00:45:37.159
that are difficult to understand.

00:45:39.159 --> 00:45:40.159
This Rosh Hashanah,

00:45:41.159 --> 00:45:42.159
it's problematic.

00:45:43.159 --> 00:45:45.159
How many days we celebrate Rosh Hashanah?

00:45:46.159 --> 00:45:47.159
Two days.

00:45:47.159 --> 00:45:48.159
But from the Torah,

00:45:48.159 --> 00:45:49.159
how many days there are?

00:45:50.159 --> 00:45:51.159
One day.

00:45:52.159 --> 00:45:53.159
This Rosh Hashanah,

00:45:53.159 --> 00:45:54.159
the first day is Shabbat.

00:45:54.159 --> 00:45:55.159
I understand, no?

00:45:56.159 --> 00:45:57.159
Shabbat.

00:45:59.159 --> 00:46:00.159
The second day,

00:46:00.159 --> 00:46:01.159
Sunday.

00:46:02.159 --> 00:46:04.159
So which day is in the Torah really?

00:46:07.159 --> 00:46:09.159
One of the most important mitzvot,

00:46:11.159 --> 00:46:12.159
blowing the shofar,

00:46:14.159 --> 00:46:15.159
is written in the Torah.

00:46:17.159 --> 00:46:18.159
Blowing the shofar.

00:46:20.159 --> 00:46:21.159
On the Day of Resurrection,

00:46:22.159 --> 00:46:23.159
we have the obligation

00:46:24.159 --> 00:46:25.159
to listen to

00:46:26.159 --> 00:46:27.159
shofar.

00:46:29.159 --> 00:46:31.159
Are we going to listen to shofar this year in Rosh Hashanah?

00:46:32.159 --> 00:46:33.159
No.

00:46:35.159 --> 00:46:36.159
Shofar, Rosh Hashanah?

00:46:37.159 --> 00:46:38.159
No.

00:46:39.159 --> 00:46:40.159
Why?

00:46:44.159 --> 00:46:46.159
How could the rabbis do such a thing?

00:46:48.159 --> 00:46:50.159
Mitzvot in the Torah!

00:46:51.159 --> 00:46:52.159
The Torah says,

00:46:52.159 --> 00:46:54.159
Yom Teruah Yirachem.

00:46:56.159 --> 00:46:58.159
The rabbis says, no, no, no, you cannot do it.

00:46:59.159 --> 00:47:00.159
Now,

00:47:01.159 --> 00:47:02.159
the worst part about it,

00:47:02.159 --> 00:47:04.159
is not only that we don't do it,

00:47:04.159 --> 00:47:06.159
we don't obey to the law of the Torah.

00:47:07.159 --> 00:47:08.159
Because an agent

00:47:09.159 --> 00:47:10.159
told me, don't.

00:47:10.159 --> 00:47:11.159
By the way, also,

00:47:11.159 --> 00:47:12.159
according to the laws of this country,

00:47:13.159 --> 00:47:14.159
and this is the law of this country,

00:47:15.159 --> 00:47:17.159
if there is a red light,

00:47:19.159 --> 00:47:20.159
and a policeman tells you,

00:47:20.159 --> 00:47:21.159
cross, go ahead,

00:47:23.159 --> 00:47:24.159
you cross to the red light, you know this?

00:47:25.159 --> 00:47:26.159
If it's a green light,

00:47:27.159 --> 00:47:28.159
and he tells you, stop,

00:47:29.159 --> 00:47:30.159
you go ahead, or you stop?

00:47:31.159 --> 00:47:32.159
One minute, alright.

00:47:33.159 --> 00:47:34.159
I want you to understand, alright?

00:47:36.159 --> 00:47:37.159
You're going to say,

00:47:37.159 --> 00:47:38.159
isn't there a red light?

00:47:39.159 --> 00:47:40.159
I'm telling you, cross the red light.

00:47:40.159 --> 00:47:41.159
You cross the red light.

00:47:43.159 --> 00:47:44.159
What's going on?

00:47:44.159 --> 00:47:45.159
Let me explain.

00:47:48.159 --> 00:47:50.159
Let's go, first, into the explanation.

00:47:52.159 --> 00:47:53.159
And if you don't understand, really,

00:47:54.159 --> 00:47:55.159
the explanation seems to be totally ridiculous.

00:47:56.159 --> 00:47:57.159
It says, why did the hachamin say,

00:47:57.159 --> 00:47:58.159
don't blow the shofar?

00:47:59.159 --> 00:48:00.159
Shemei yikahen,

00:48:00.159 --> 00:48:02.159
ya'avilenu dalet amod meshut harabim.

00:48:05.159 --> 00:48:06.159
It says, maybe this guy,

00:48:07.159 --> 00:48:08.159
he doesn't know how to blow the shofar well,

00:48:09.159 --> 00:48:10.159
he would take it to somebody

00:48:11.159 --> 00:48:12.159
that knows how to blow the shofar,

00:48:14.159 --> 00:48:15.159
and he would take it,

00:48:15.159 --> 00:48:17.159
Shabbat, would take him four steps

00:48:19.159 --> 00:48:20.159
through the street,

00:48:22.159 --> 00:48:23.159
and therefore, it's better

00:48:24.159 --> 00:48:25.159
not to blow the shofar.

00:48:26.159 --> 00:48:27.159
That's the reason.

00:48:28.159 --> 00:48:29.159
Now, you could explain to people,

00:48:30.159 --> 00:48:31.159
don't take it.

00:48:32.159 --> 00:48:33.159
Most people

00:48:34.159 --> 00:48:35.159
don't know how to blow the shofar,

00:48:35.159 --> 00:48:36.159
they come to the synagogue, they listen.

00:48:37.159 --> 00:48:38.159
The rabbi from the synagogue,

00:48:40.159 --> 00:48:41.159
certainly he's not going to take it

00:48:42.159 --> 00:48:43.159
in the street.

00:48:44.159 --> 00:48:45.159
As a matter of fact,

00:48:45.159 --> 00:48:46.159
he's not going to let others

00:48:46.159 --> 00:48:47.159
take it in the street.

00:48:48.159 --> 00:48:49.159
He said, no,

00:48:50.159 --> 00:48:51.159
don't do it.

00:48:51.159 --> 00:48:52.159
Why?

00:48:52.159 --> 00:48:53.159
Shemei yikahen,

00:48:53.159 --> 00:48:54.159
ya'avilenu dalet amod meshut harabim.

00:48:55.159 --> 00:48:56.159
The explanation

00:48:58.159 --> 00:48:59.159
is worse

00:49:00.159 --> 00:49:01.159
than no explanation at all.

00:49:04.159 --> 00:49:05.159
Now,

00:49:06.159 --> 00:49:07.159
what I'm telling you,

00:49:07.159 --> 00:49:08.159
the next sentence or two,

00:49:08.159 --> 00:49:09.159
that's mine,

00:49:09.159 --> 00:49:10.159
it comes from me,

00:49:10.159 --> 00:49:11.159
and then it comes from

00:49:11.159 --> 00:49:12.159
Rabbi Yavid Yadav.

00:49:12.159 --> 00:49:13.159
One other thing I observed

00:49:14.159 --> 00:49:15.159
through Talmud,

00:49:15.159 --> 00:49:16.159
that for the Jews,

00:49:18.159 --> 00:49:19.159
in those days,

00:49:19.159 --> 00:49:20.159
more than nowadays,

00:49:22.159 --> 00:49:23.159
to blow the shofar was like

00:49:24.159 --> 00:49:25.159
the epitome of everything.

00:49:26.159 --> 00:49:27.159
If you don't listen to the shofar,

00:49:27.159 --> 00:49:28.159
it's like

00:49:29.159 --> 00:49:30.159
many Jews,

00:49:30.159 --> 00:49:31.159
they're not delicious and anything,

00:49:31.159 --> 00:49:32.159
but to listen to Kalnidra,

00:49:32.159 --> 00:49:33.159
they come to Kalnidra, you know?

00:49:34.159 --> 00:49:35.159
For them, the shofar

00:49:35.159 --> 00:49:36.159
was even more than that.

00:49:36.159 --> 00:49:37.159
I mean, if you don't listen

00:49:37.159 --> 00:49:38.159
to the shofar,

00:49:38.159 --> 00:49:39.159
it's like, I don't know,

00:49:39.159 --> 00:49:40.159
you could eat pork,

00:49:40.159 --> 00:49:41.159
you could do this,

00:49:41.159 --> 00:49:42.159
you could make

00:49:42.159 --> 00:49:43.159
mehal shabbat,

00:49:43.159 --> 00:49:44.159
everything.

00:49:44.159 --> 00:49:45.159
But, you know,

00:49:45.159 --> 00:49:46.159
listen to the shofar.

00:49:46.159 --> 00:49:47.159
You listen to the shofar,

00:49:47.159 --> 00:49:48.159
everything is going to be alright.

00:49:48.159 --> 00:49:49.159
That's what the mind

00:49:49.159 --> 00:49:50.159
of the Jews,

00:49:50.159 --> 00:49:51.159
it occurs.

00:49:52.159 --> 00:49:53.159
Now,

00:49:53.159 --> 00:49:54.159
one minute.

00:49:57.159 --> 00:49:58.159
Rabbi Yavid Yadav explains like this.

00:50:00.159 --> 00:50:01.159
The reason

00:50:02.159 --> 00:50:03.159
why

00:50:03.159 --> 00:50:04.159
the rabbis

00:50:06.159 --> 00:50:07.159
prohibited

00:50:07.159 --> 00:50:08.159
to blow the shofar

00:50:09.159 --> 00:50:10.159
this Rosh Hashanah,

00:50:11.159 --> 00:50:12.159
abiding in Shalom,

00:50:13.159 --> 00:50:14.159
is for pedagogical reasons.

00:50:16.159 --> 00:50:17.159
Genius.

00:50:17.159 --> 00:50:18.159
Really genius.

00:50:21.159 --> 00:50:22.159
Jews,

00:50:23.159 --> 00:50:24.159
then

00:50:25.159 --> 00:50:26.159
and now

00:50:27.159 --> 00:50:28.159
always observe Shabbat.

00:50:30.159 --> 00:50:31.159
They observe Shabbat.

00:50:32.159 --> 00:50:33.159
They will not strike a match

00:50:33.159 --> 00:50:34.159
or this.

00:50:35.159 --> 00:50:36.159
No matter this or that.

00:50:37.159 --> 00:50:38.159
But to carry?

00:50:39.159 --> 00:50:40.159
Come on.

00:50:40.159 --> 00:50:41.159
Don't tell me that this is forbidden.

00:50:42.159 --> 00:50:44.159
People carry their sweets.

00:50:46.159 --> 00:50:47.159
The people cannot understand

00:50:48.159 --> 00:50:49.159
that this is prohibited.

00:50:50.159 --> 00:50:51.159
Just like you are prohibited

00:50:51.159 --> 00:50:52.159
to strike a match.

00:50:54.159 --> 00:50:55.159
It's prohibited to carry your sweets.

00:50:55.159 --> 00:50:56.159
Shabbat is prohibited.

00:50:57.159 --> 00:50:58.159
Where should I be?

00:50:58.159 --> 00:50:59.159
That's prohibited.

00:51:00.159 --> 00:51:01.159
Jews observe everything

00:51:01.159 --> 00:51:02.159
on Shabbat,

00:51:02.159 --> 00:51:03.159
except

00:51:05.159 --> 00:51:06.159
carrying.

00:51:08.159 --> 00:51:09.159
That's why, for example,

00:51:09.159 --> 00:51:10.159
I have Shalom.

00:51:10.159 --> 00:51:11.159
I don't want to say nothing

00:51:11.159 --> 00:51:12.159
about what to do

00:51:12.159 --> 00:51:13.159
and what not to do.

00:51:13.159 --> 00:51:14.159
When I was in Brooklyn,

00:51:14.159 --> 00:51:15.159
I was very much in favor

00:51:15.159 --> 00:51:16.159
to make Eilub.

00:51:17.159 --> 00:51:18.159
Because, I say,

00:51:18.159 --> 00:51:19.159
anyhow people are carrying,

00:51:19.159 --> 00:51:20.159
at least let them carry

00:51:20.159 --> 00:51:21.159
with the Eilub

00:51:21.159 --> 00:51:22.159
that they may not make Havon.

00:51:23.159 --> 00:51:24.159
But, I know,

00:51:24.159 --> 00:51:25.159
every community has its own policy,

00:51:25.159 --> 00:51:26.159
whatever it is.

00:51:26.159 --> 00:51:27.159
But,

00:51:27.159 --> 00:51:28.159
everybody carries.

00:51:28.159 --> 00:51:29.159
Even people are Shomer Shabbat,

00:51:31.159 --> 00:51:32.159
without knowing it,

00:51:32.159 --> 00:51:33.159
they are Mechalesh Shabbat

00:51:33.159 --> 00:51:34.159
because they carry.

00:51:36.159 --> 00:51:37.159
They say,

00:51:37.159 --> 00:51:38.159
but Baba,

00:51:38.159 --> 00:51:39.159
I only carry a handkerchief.

00:51:39.159 --> 00:51:40.159
It's a sword,

00:51:40.159 --> 00:51:41.159
what could you do?

00:51:41.159 --> 00:51:42.159
Only this,

00:51:42.159 --> 00:51:43.159
only this.

00:51:44.159 --> 00:51:46.159
How can you teach the people

00:51:47.159 --> 00:51:49.159
that you are not permitted

00:51:49.159 --> 00:51:51.159
to carry on Shabbat?

00:51:51.159 --> 00:51:52.159
There's only one way.

00:51:54.159 --> 00:51:56.159
This Rosh Hashanah,

00:51:56.159 --> 00:51:58.159
everybody comes,

00:51:59.159 --> 00:52:00.159
they want to listen to what?

00:52:01.159 --> 00:52:02.159
Not this Chazan,

00:52:02.159 --> 00:52:03.159
not this,

00:52:03.159 --> 00:52:04.159
not that,

00:52:04.159 --> 00:52:05.159
not even Sarihod,

00:52:05.159 --> 00:52:06.159
but they want to listen.

00:52:08.159 --> 00:52:09.159
Comes the Rabbi,

00:52:09.159 --> 00:52:10.159
makes an announcement,

00:52:10.159 --> 00:52:11.159
ladies and gentlemen,

00:52:11.159 --> 00:52:12.159
no Shofar today.

00:52:13.159 --> 00:52:14.159
Why?

00:52:16.159 --> 00:52:17.159
Because,

00:52:18.159 --> 00:52:19.159
maybe,

00:52:19.159 --> 00:52:20.159
somebody

00:52:20.159 --> 00:52:21.159
may carry a Shofar,

00:52:22.159 --> 00:52:23.159
Arba Amod,

00:52:23.159 --> 00:52:25.159
for four yards,

00:52:26.159 --> 00:52:27.159
in the Shute Rabbin.

00:52:28.159 --> 00:52:30.159
When the most sacred Misbah,

00:52:31.159 --> 00:52:32.159
in the minds of the,

00:52:32.159 --> 00:52:33.159
in the minds of the,

00:52:34.159 --> 00:52:35.159
of the community,

00:52:37.159 --> 00:52:38.159
is annulled,

00:52:43.159 --> 00:52:44.159
postponed,

00:52:45.159 --> 00:52:46.159
because,

00:52:47.159 --> 00:52:48.159
maybe,

00:52:48.159 --> 00:52:50.159
someone may take it

00:52:51.159 --> 00:52:52.159
through the streets.

00:52:54.159 --> 00:52:56.159
Then the people begin to understand

00:52:57.159 --> 00:52:58.159
the severity

00:52:59.159 --> 00:53:00.159
of one Avon,

00:53:02.159 --> 00:53:03.159
that unfortunately,

00:53:04.159 --> 00:53:06.159
people don't pay attention about.

00:53:06.159 --> 00:53:07.159
So,

00:53:07.159 --> 00:53:10.159
when the Rabbis make those Gezerot,

00:53:10.159 --> 00:53:11.159
those laws,

00:53:12.159 --> 00:53:13.159
that apparently,

00:53:16.159 --> 00:53:17.159
are shocking,

00:53:19.159 --> 00:53:20.159
Rabbi David Neto goes,

00:53:20.159 --> 00:53:21.159
explaining,

00:53:22.159 --> 00:53:23.159
explaining,

00:53:24.159 --> 00:53:25.159
that they have a function.

00:53:25.159 --> 00:53:26.159
I want to

00:53:27.159 --> 00:53:29.159
bring another example,

00:53:29.159 --> 00:53:30.159
that was discussed by him.

00:53:32.159 --> 00:53:33.159
In the Torah,

00:53:33.159 --> 00:53:34.159
says,

00:53:36.159 --> 00:53:38.159
it is prohibited

00:53:39.159 --> 00:53:40.159
to take interest.

00:53:41.159 --> 00:53:42.159
When a Jew

00:53:42.159 --> 00:53:44.159
lends money to another Jew,

00:53:46.159 --> 00:53:47.159
he should do it gratis,

00:53:47.159 --> 00:53:49.159
as an act of Gimilut Hasadim,

00:53:51.159 --> 00:53:53.159
and he should not take interest.

00:53:53.159 --> 00:53:55.159
He should not take interest.

00:53:57.159 --> 00:53:58.159
Many Jews,

00:54:00.159 --> 00:54:01.159
that's called rebid,

00:54:01.159 --> 00:54:02.159
it is prohibited,

00:54:02.159 --> 00:54:03.159
by Jewish law,

00:54:03.159 --> 00:54:04.159
it is prohibited to take interest.

00:54:05.159 --> 00:54:07.159
Many Jews coming from Spain and Portugal,

00:54:09.159 --> 00:54:10.159
they read only the Bible,

00:54:10.159 --> 00:54:11.159
because they,

00:54:11.159 --> 00:54:12.159
you know,

00:54:12.159 --> 00:54:13.159
they were Anusim,

00:54:13.159 --> 00:54:14.159
they were conversants,

00:54:14.159 --> 00:54:15.159
they could not read the Talmud.

00:54:16.159 --> 00:54:17.159
They were shocked,

00:54:17.159 --> 00:54:18.159
when they came to

00:54:18.159 --> 00:54:19.159
Europe,

00:54:19.159 --> 00:54:20.159
Italy,

00:54:20.159 --> 00:54:21.159
England,

00:54:21.159 --> 00:54:22.159
Amsterdam,

00:54:22.159 --> 00:54:23.159
went to Jewish committee,

00:54:23.159 --> 00:54:24.159
and they see that,

00:54:24.159 --> 00:54:25.159
you go,

00:54:25.159 --> 00:54:26.159
if you want to borrow money,

00:54:26.159 --> 00:54:27.159
you go to the Rabbi,

00:54:27.159 --> 00:54:28.159
he gives you something,

00:54:28.159 --> 00:54:29.159
you write something in a paper,

00:54:30.159 --> 00:54:31.159
you sign it,

00:54:31.159 --> 00:54:33.159
you could lend with interest.

00:54:34.159 --> 00:54:35.159
When they saw such a thing,

00:54:35.159 --> 00:54:36.159
Heteroska,

00:54:36.159 --> 00:54:37.159
Shetan Heteroska,

00:54:38.159 --> 00:54:39.159
when they saw such a thing,

00:54:39.159 --> 00:54:40.159
they said,

00:54:40.159 --> 00:54:41.159
the Rabbis are

00:54:41.159 --> 00:54:43.159
manipulating the law.

00:54:46.159 --> 00:54:47.159
What the Rabbis are doing,

00:54:49.159 --> 00:54:50.159
is contrary to the Torah.

00:54:52.159 --> 00:54:53.159
Nothing like a Shofar.

00:54:53.159 --> 00:54:54.159
The Shofar,

00:54:54.159 --> 00:54:55.159
it tells you,

00:54:55.159 --> 00:54:56.159
don't blow it.

00:54:57.159 --> 00:54:58.159
You are passive.

00:54:59.159 --> 00:55:00.159
Here, it says,

00:55:00.159 --> 00:55:01.159
go ahead and lend,

00:55:01.159 --> 00:55:02.159
and take interest.

00:55:02.159 --> 00:55:03.159
Kumbaseh.

00:55:06.159 --> 00:55:07.159
What is the meaning?

00:55:08.159 --> 00:55:09.159
How could the Rabbis

00:55:10.159 --> 00:55:11.159
go against what's written in the Torah?

00:55:11.159 --> 00:55:12.159
The Torah says,

00:55:12.159 --> 00:55:13.159
don't take interest.

00:55:14.159 --> 00:55:16.159
The explanation is so simple,

00:55:17.159 --> 00:55:19.159
and I don't want to mention names,

00:55:20.159 --> 00:55:21.159
but I had a discussion

00:55:21.159 --> 00:55:23.159
with a man who is a judge,

00:55:24.159 --> 00:55:25.159
a religious judge,

00:55:25.159 --> 00:55:26.159
a Dayan in Israel.

00:55:27.159 --> 00:55:28.159
He himself didn't understand

00:55:28.159 --> 00:55:29.159
what the law is.

00:55:30.159 --> 00:55:31.159
And I told him,

00:55:31.159 --> 00:55:32.159
read in the Rabbi Tavini,

00:55:32.159 --> 00:55:33.159
the explanation.

00:55:34.159 --> 00:55:35.159
Because the explanation is so simple,

00:55:36.159 --> 00:55:37.159
but sometimes people,

00:55:37.159 --> 00:55:38.159
not everybody is acquainted even,

00:55:39.159 --> 00:55:40.159
you know,

00:55:40.159 --> 00:55:41.159
the simplest explanations

00:55:41.159 --> 00:55:42.159
are the most beautiful

00:55:42.159 --> 00:55:43.159
and the most difficult

00:55:43.159 --> 00:55:44.159
to get about,

00:55:44.159 --> 00:55:45.159
to find.

00:55:45.159 --> 00:55:46.159
It's something very simple.

00:55:48.159 --> 00:55:49.159
Yes,

00:55:49.159 --> 00:55:50.159
the Torah prohibits us

00:55:50.159 --> 00:55:51.159
to take interest.

00:55:52.159 --> 00:55:53.159
But you have to understand

00:55:53.159 --> 00:55:54.159
Jewish law.

00:55:55.159 --> 00:55:56.159
According to Jewish law,

00:55:57.159 --> 00:55:58.159
if I borrow

00:55:59.159 --> 00:56:00.159
five dollars from you,

00:56:03.159 --> 00:56:04.159
this debt

00:56:04.159 --> 00:56:05.159
is forever.

00:56:06.159 --> 00:56:07.159
I cannot bankrupt.

00:56:08.159 --> 00:56:09.159
No matter what I do,

00:56:09.159 --> 00:56:10.159
I owe you this five dollars.

00:56:12.159 --> 00:56:13.159
And,

00:56:13.159 --> 00:56:14.159
if the debtor

00:56:14.159 --> 00:56:15.159
dies,

00:56:16.159 --> 00:56:17.159
the heirs have to pay the debt.

00:56:17.159 --> 00:56:18.159
They just have to pay the debt.

00:56:20.159 --> 00:56:21.159
And if they die and so on,

00:56:21.159 --> 00:56:22.159
the property,

00:56:22.159 --> 00:56:23.159
you take the property and so on.

00:56:23.159 --> 00:56:24.159
The debt,

00:56:24.159 --> 00:56:25.159
once you take a debt

00:56:25.159 --> 00:56:26.159
from somebody,

00:56:29.159 --> 00:56:30.159
no matter what happens,

00:56:33.159 --> 00:56:35.159
you must pay the debt.

00:56:37.159 --> 00:56:38.159
Law,

00:56:38.159 --> 00:56:39.159
the law does not recognize

00:56:39.159 --> 00:56:40.159
any excuse

00:56:41.159 --> 00:56:42.159
for default.

00:56:44.159 --> 00:56:45.159
Now,

00:56:45.159 --> 00:56:46.159
therefore,

00:56:46.159 --> 00:56:47.159
if I

00:56:47.159 --> 00:56:48.159
take five dollars from you

00:56:48.159 --> 00:56:49.159
as a loan,

00:56:52.159 --> 00:56:53.159
and then I give you

00:56:53.159 --> 00:56:54.159
five cents,

00:56:54.159 --> 00:56:55.159
ten cents,

00:56:55.159 --> 00:56:56.159
whatever it is,

00:56:56.159 --> 00:56:57.159
a month, a day,

00:56:57.159 --> 00:56:58.159
for interest,

00:56:58.159 --> 00:56:59.159
that is considered interest

00:56:59.159 --> 00:57:00.159
because your loan

00:57:00.159 --> 00:57:01.159
is guaranteed by the Torah.

00:57:02.159 --> 00:57:03.159
This guy is going to pay.

00:57:05.159 --> 00:57:06.159
You are having

00:57:07.159 --> 00:57:08.159
a profit

00:57:09.159 --> 00:57:11.159
without risking anything

00:57:13.159 --> 00:57:14.159
because

00:57:14.159 --> 00:57:15.159
your payment

00:57:15.159 --> 00:57:16.159
is guaranteed.

00:57:17.159 --> 00:57:18.159
I have to pay you the debt.

00:57:19.159 --> 00:57:20.159
Now,

00:57:21.159 --> 00:57:22.159
when you go to the rabbi,

00:57:22.159 --> 00:57:23.159
and you say,

00:57:23.159 --> 00:57:24.159
rabbi,

00:57:24.159 --> 00:57:25.159
would you do this?

00:57:25.159 --> 00:57:26.159
He makes you sign something

00:57:26.159 --> 00:57:27.159
and you read what is there.

00:57:28.159 --> 00:57:29.159
In point of fact,

00:57:29.159 --> 00:57:30.159
you are saying,

00:57:31.159 --> 00:57:32.159
she wants to take interest from me.

00:57:33.159 --> 00:57:34.159
You give me a loan of five dollars.

00:57:35.159 --> 00:57:36.159
She says the following,

00:57:37.159 --> 00:57:38.159
that the interest

00:57:38.159 --> 00:57:39.159
is part

00:57:41.159 --> 00:57:42.159
of the profits

00:57:42.159 --> 00:57:43.159
that I am going to generate

00:57:43.159 --> 00:57:44.159
with this five dollars.

00:57:46.159 --> 00:57:47.159
You know what does it mean

00:57:47.159 --> 00:57:48.159
according to the law?

00:57:49.159 --> 00:57:50.159
It means like this,

00:57:50.159 --> 00:57:51.159
that

00:57:51.159 --> 00:57:52.159
if I

00:57:52.159 --> 00:57:53.159
lose the money,

00:57:53.159 --> 00:57:54.159
I, the one who borrowed

00:57:54.159 --> 00:57:55.159
the five dollars,

00:57:56.159 --> 00:57:57.159
in a legitimate,

00:57:58.159 --> 00:57:59.159
and there is laws and so on,

00:57:59.159 --> 00:58:00.159
that what we are investing,

00:58:00.159 --> 00:58:01.159
why I cannot invest,

00:58:01.159 --> 00:58:02.159
but in a legitimate investment,

00:58:04.159 --> 00:58:05.159
I invest this five dollars

00:58:08.159 --> 00:58:09.159
in a legitimate way,

00:58:09.159 --> 00:58:10.159
in a legitimate way,

00:58:12.159 --> 00:58:13.159
and I lost the money,

00:58:15.159 --> 00:58:16.159
I don't have to pay you.

00:58:18.159 --> 00:58:19.159
Therefore,

00:58:19.159 --> 00:58:20.159
interest is

00:58:21.159 --> 00:58:22.159
prohibited

00:58:22.159 --> 00:58:23.159
when I have,

00:58:23.159 --> 00:58:25.159
my law is guaranteed,

00:58:26.159 --> 00:58:28.159
and there is no possibility of loss.

00:58:30.159 --> 00:58:31.159
But if the law is contracted

00:58:31.159 --> 00:58:32.159
in such a way,

00:58:35.159 --> 00:58:37.159
that in a legitimate investment,

00:58:39.159 --> 00:58:41.159
I lose the principal,

00:58:43.159 --> 00:58:44.159
which means the creditor

00:58:44.159 --> 00:58:46.159
is taking a risk,

00:58:49.159 --> 00:58:50.159
then

00:58:50.159 --> 00:58:51.159
the interest

00:58:51.159 --> 00:58:52.159
is legitimate,

00:58:52.159 --> 00:58:53.159
is permitted.

00:58:53.159 --> 00:58:54.159
That is not considered interest,

00:58:54.159 --> 00:58:55.159
that is considered rewach,

00:58:55.159 --> 00:58:56.159
not neshech,

00:58:57.159 --> 00:58:58.159
rewach.

00:58:58.159 --> 00:59:00.159
One is considered interest,

00:59:02.159 --> 00:59:03.159
and it is prohibited,

00:59:04.159 --> 00:59:06.159
and whenever you take in a risk

00:59:07.159 --> 00:59:08.159
in the principal

00:59:09.159 --> 00:59:10.159
through a transaction,

00:59:11.159 --> 00:59:12.159
that is not considered interest,

00:59:13.159 --> 00:59:14.159
it is considered gain,

00:59:15.159 --> 00:59:16.159
and that is permitted.

00:59:17.159 --> 00:59:18.159
So, what the

00:59:18.159 --> 00:59:19.159
Chagham David Nietzsche Talam Shalom does,

00:59:19.159 --> 00:59:21.159
is takes all those difficult laws,

00:59:24.159 --> 00:59:25.159
instituted by the rabbis,

00:59:26.159 --> 00:59:27.159
examines one by one,

00:59:29.159 --> 00:59:31.159
and try to explain to you,

00:59:33.159 --> 00:59:35.159
what is the function of the law

00:59:37.159 --> 00:59:38.159
why those things that you think are

00:59:40.159 --> 00:59:41.159
illogical,

00:59:41.159 --> 00:59:43.159
what is the logic of this law,

00:59:44.159 --> 00:59:46.159
so that in this third dialogue,

00:59:47.159 --> 00:59:49.159
he goes on analyzing

00:59:51.159 --> 00:59:53.159
not the structure of the rabbinic authority,

00:59:53.159 --> 00:59:55.159
but the actual things that it did.

00:59:56.159 --> 00:59:57.159
I want to go,

00:59:58.159 --> 00:59:59.159
I think I have time,

01:00:01.159 --> 01:00:02.159
to a fantastic question that he asked,

01:00:04.159 --> 01:00:05.159
and I have an answer.

01:00:05.159 --> 01:00:06.159
The answer I got it today,

01:00:07.159 --> 01:00:08.159
in a fax.

01:00:08.159 --> 01:00:09.159
Somebody faxed me the answer,

01:00:10.159 --> 01:00:11.159
my son faxed me the answer.

01:00:13.159 --> 01:00:14.159
I wanted to give you the answer properly,

01:00:16.159 --> 01:00:17.159
and before this,

01:00:18.159 --> 01:00:19.159
I called up,

01:00:20.159 --> 01:00:21.159
yesterday I called my son,

01:00:21.159 --> 01:00:22.159
I said, do me a favor,

01:00:22.159 --> 01:00:24.159
I need this, and this, and this, and this.

01:00:24.159 --> 01:00:25.159
And he sent me the thing.

01:00:27.159 --> 01:00:28.159
The question that

01:00:28.159 --> 01:00:29.159
Rabbi David Nietzsche asked,

01:00:30.159 --> 01:00:31.159
is a question that many Christians,

01:00:32.159 --> 01:00:33.159
many Jews who were not exposed

01:00:34.159 --> 01:00:35.159
sufficiently to Judaism, ask.

01:00:37.159 --> 01:00:38.159
Look at the Torah.

01:00:39.159 --> 01:00:40.159
The five books of Moses.

01:00:41.159 --> 01:00:42.159
So simple.

01:00:44.159 --> 01:00:45.159
And what the rabbis had done?

01:00:47.159 --> 01:00:48.159
Volumes, and volumes, and volumes,

01:00:50.159 --> 01:00:51.159
and volumes, and volumes of Torah.

01:00:53.159 --> 01:00:54.159
We cannot understand a word.

01:00:55.159 --> 01:00:57.159
Just let me read how much is sufficient.

01:00:59.159 --> 01:01:00.159
What I find?

01:01:00.159 --> 01:01:01.159
I find how much is, you know,

01:01:02.159 --> 01:01:03.159
small little book,

01:01:04.159 --> 01:01:05.159
then next to it,

01:01:05.159 --> 01:01:06.159
the Mishnayot, alright,

01:01:08.159 --> 01:01:09.159
another book,

01:01:10.159 --> 01:01:11.159
then the Talmud, 20 volumes,

01:01:14.159 --> 01:01:15.159
then the early commentators,

01:01:18.159 --> 01:01:19.159
then the Shulchan Aruch,

01:01:20.159 --> 01:01:21.159
and around the Shulchan Aruch

01:01:21.159 --> 01:01:22.159
you have more commentaries,

01:01:23.159 --> 01:01:24.159
and commentaries,

01:01:24.159 --> 01:01:25.159
and the commentaries,

01:01:26.159 --> 01:01:27.159
and then that's not sufficient.

01:01:28.159 --> 01:01:29.159
Then you have another

01:01:29.159 --> 01:01:30.159
Sheilutu Chuvotu Spanza.

01:01:31.159 --> 01:01:32.159
People who summarize the Spanza.

01:01:34.159 --> 01:01:35.159
Now we have it in computers.

01:01:37.159 --> 01:01:38.159
What's going on?

01:01:39.159 --> 01:01:40.159
These rabbis,

01:01:40.159 --> 01:01:41.159
Selechah,

01:01:41.159 --> 01:01:42.159
went wild!

01:01:44.159 --> 01:01:45.159
You know?

01:01:45.159 --> 01:01:46.159
There is no end!

01:01:49.159 --> 01:01:50.159
Rabbi David Nieto,

01:01:51.159 --> 01:01:52.159
this question was asked to him

01:01:52.159 --> 01:01:53.159
by the king.

01:01:53.159 --> 01:01:54.159
It's a dialogue between the king,

01:01:54.159 --> 01:01:55.159
the Kuzari,

01:01:55.159 --> 01:01:56.159
and the rabbi,

01:01:57.159 --> 01:01:58.159
and the king,

01:01:58.159 --> 01:01:59.159
and the rabbi.

01:01:59.159 --> 01:02:00.159
And the rabbi,

01:02:00.159 --> 01:02:01.159
as a question says,

01:02:02.159 --> 01:02:03.159
my lord and king,

01:02:04.159 --> 01:02:06.159
when you issue a tax law,

01:02:12.159 --> 01:02:13.159
do your people

01:02:14.159 --> 01:02:15.159
study the law?

01:02:18.159 --> 01:02:19.159
He says,

01:02:19.159 --> 01:02:21.159
well, my lord and king,

01:02:22.159 --> 01:02:23.159
if your law,

01:02:24.159 --> 01:02:25.159
the tax law,

01:02:25.159 --> 01:02:26.159
the tax law,

01:02:28.159 --> 01:02:30.159
is studied so meticulously,

01:02:31.159 --> 01:02:32.159
and is written, after all,

01:02:32.159 --> 01:02:33.159
by a human being,

01:02:34.159 --> 01:02:35.159
why the Torah

01:02:36.159 --> 01:02:37.159
should not be studied

01:02:37.159 --> 01:02:38.159
as meticulously?

01:02:41.159 --> 01:02:42.159
What does he say?

01:02:43.159 --> 01:02:44.159
It doesn't make much sense.

01:02:45.159 --> 01:02:46.159
But my son

01:02:46.159 --> 01:02:48.159
is a tax attorney.

01:02:51.159 --> 01:02:52.159
And he's a rabbi.

01:02:52.159 --> 01:02:54.159
But I ask him exactly,

01:02:54.159 --> 01:02:55.159
because I know,

01:02:56.159 --> 01:02:57.159
and I teach law,

01:02:57.159 --> 01:02:58.159
and I taught law at Chicago,

01:02:58.159 --> 01:02:59.159
and so on.

01:03:00.159 --> 01:03:01.159
I did a PhD,

01:03:01.159 --> 01:03:02.159
a doctorate program,

01:03:02.159 --> 01:03:03.159
MA programs.

01:03:03.159 --> 01:03:04.159
But I know that

01:03:05.159 --> 01:03:06.159
David Nieto,

01:03:06.159 --> 01:03:07.159
when he used the word tax,

01:03:07.159 --> 01:03:08.159
he knew what he was doing.

01:03:09.159 --> 01:03:10.159
All right?

01:03:11.159 --> 01:03:12.159
And I say,

01:03:13.159 --> 01:03:15.159
tell me how it goes.

01:03:15.159 --> 01:03:16.159
He says,

01:03:16.159 --> 01:03:17.159
all right,

01:03:17.159 --> 01:03:18.159
because I know that.

01:03:18.159 --> 01:03:19.159
He says,

01:03:19.159 --> 01:03:20.159
he writes to me,

01:03:20.159 --> 01:03:21.159
the Internal Revenue Code,

01:03:21.159 --> 01:03:22.159
first they have the Internal Revenue Code,

01:03:22.159 --> 01:03:23.159
which is one volume,

01:03:25.159 --> 01:03:26.159
and this is the law

01:03:26.159 --> 01:03:29.159
as the Code is enacted

01:03:29.159 --> 01:03:31.159
by a federal legislator,

01:03:31.159 --> 01:03:32.159
which is the Congress.

01:03:32.159 --> 01:03:33.159
And this is one,

01:03:33.159 --> 01:03:34.159
only one volume.

01:03:34.159 --> 01:03:35.159
All right?

01:03:36.159 --> 01:03:37.159
After, and he says,

01:03:37.159 --> 01:03:39.159
it is the Torah Shevichtav

01:03:39.159 --> 01:03:40.159
of tax law.

01:03:40.159 --> 01:03:41.159
All right?

01:03:41.159 --> 01:03:42.159
That's like,

01:03:42.159 --> 01:03:43.159
there's one volume,

01:03:43.159 --> 01:03:44.159
this is by the Congress.

01:03:44.159 --> 01:03:45.159
One volume.

01:03:45.159 --> 01:03:46.159
All right?

01:03:46.159 --> 01:03:48.159
Then there are the regulations.

01:03:49.159 --> 01:03:51.159
The Treasury Department

01:03:52.159 --> 01:03:53.159
interprets the tax law.

01:03:53.159 --> 01:03:55.159
You cannot interpret the tax law.

01:03:57.159 --> 01:03:58.159
You know what it is?

01:03:58.159 --> 01:04:00.159
You cannot interpret the tax law

01:04:00.159 --> 01:04:01.159
enacted by the Congress,

01:04:01.159 --> 01:04:03.159
by the US Congress,

01:04:03.159 --> 01:04:05.159
is interpreted

01:04:05.159 --> 01:04:07.159
by the Treasury Department.

01:04:09.159 --> 01:04:11.159
And the Treasury Department

01:04:11.159 --> 01:04:13.159
has five volumes

01:04:14.159 --> 01:04:16.159
under one volume.

01:04:16.159 --> 01:04:17.159
One minute.

01:04:18.159 --> 01:04:19.159
Then,

01:04:20.159 --> 01:04:21.159
that is,

01:04:21.159 --> 01:04:22.159
that is

01:04:22.159 --> 01:04:24.159
the Treasury Department.

01:04:24.159 --> 01:04:26.159
But then there's a third kind of book

01:04:26.159 --> 01:04:29.159
called Revenue Rulings,

01:04:30.159 --> 01:04:32.159
which is the way

01:04:33.159 --> 01:04:34.159
the Court

01:04:35.159 --> 01:04:36.159
interprets

01:04:36.159 --> 01:04:38.159
what the Treasury says.

01:04:40.159 --> 01:04:41.159
All right?

01:04:41.159 --> 01:04:43.159
A Revenue Ruling

01:04:43.159 --> 01:04:46.159
is the Internal Revenue Service

01:04:46.159 --> 01:04:47.159
ruling,

01:04:47.159 --> 01:04:49.159
the Court of the Internal Revenue

01:04:49.159 --> 01:04:51.159
in actual matters pending before them.

01:04:52.159 --> 01:04:53.159
All right?

01:04:53.159 --> 01:04:54.159
For example,

01:04:54.159 --> 01:04:55.159
a taxpayer takes a deduction

01:04:55.159 --> 01:04:58.159
basing himself on a code section,

01:04:58.159 --> 01:05:00.159
it has to be approved

01:05:02.159 --> 01:05:04.159
by the Revenue Rulings.

01:05:04.159 --> 01:05:05.159
If I say,

01:05:05.159 --> 01:05:06.159
I interpret this as,

01:05:06.159 --> 01:05:07.159
no, no, no, no, no,

01:05:07.159 --> 01:05:09.159
before you take the deduction,

01:05:10.159 --> 01:05:11.159
this deduction

01:05:12.159 --> 01:05:13.159
has to be approved

01:05:13.159 --> 01:05:16.159
by the Revenue Rulings.

01:05:16.159 --> 01:05:17.159
Fine.

01:05:17.159 --> 01:05:19.159
Then there's a fourth thing,

01:05:19.159 --> 01:05:20.159
which is

01:05:20.159 --> 01:05:22.159
Private Letter Rulings,

01:05:23.159 --> 01:05:25.159
where the taxpayer is unsure,

01:05:25.159 --> 01:05:27.159
he doesn't know what the law is,

01:05:27.159 --> 01:05:29.159
he sends a she'elaw chuvah,

01:05:29.159 --> 01:05:30.159
she'elotu chuvot,

01:05:30.159 --> 01:05:32.159
to the tax revenue.

01:05:32.159 --> 01:05:35.159
He makes a she'elaw chuvah to the service,

01:05:35.159 --> 01:05:37.159
and if the service feels that the issue in question

01:05:37.159 --> 01:05:39.159
is significant and intelligent,

01:05:40.159 --> 01:05:41.159
they may, at the restriction,

01:05:41.159 --> 01:05:43.159
issue a pesagdin.

01:05:43.159 --> 01:05:44.159
That's the fourth.

01:05:44.159 --> 01:05:45.159
One second.

01:05:45.159 --> 01:05:46.159
Then there is

01:05:46.159 --> 01:05:47.159
fifth,

01:05:47.159 --> 01:05:50.159
the Tax Court and Federal Court.

01:05:52.159 --> 01:05:53.159
Best

01:05:53.159 --> 01:05:54.159
as possible.

01:05:56.159 --> 01:05:57.159
Do I have to follow them?

01:05:59.159 --> 01:06:01.159
That's an important question.

01:06:02.159 --> 01:06:04.159
And basically the answer of Rabbi David Neto is

01:06:04.159 --> 01:06:05.159
yes.

01:06:06.159 --> 01:06:08.159
Because they are the agents

01:06:08.159 --> 01:06:09.159
of Bola Golan.

01:06:10.159 --> 01:06:13.159
And when you are disobeying the rabbis,

01:06:14.159 --> 01:06:16.159
when I disobey,

01:06:16.159 --> 01:06:18.159
if I raise my hand

01:06:19.159 --> 01:06:21.159
against a police in duty,

01:06:24.159 --> 01:06:27.159
I will be punished in different way

01:06:28.159 --> 01:06:31.159
than if I raise my hand against another human being.

01:06:32.159 --> 01:06:34.159
Or against the same policeman when he is not in duty.

01:06:34.159 --> 01:06:36.159
Because he represents the law.

01:06:36.159 --> 01:06:38.159
The hachamim represent the law.

01:06:40.159 --> 01:06:41.159
And

01:06:41.159 --> 01:06:43.159
we testify to this

01:06:43.159 --> 01:06:44.159
every time

01:06:46.159 --> 01:06:47.159
that we make Eruvim

01:06:48.159 --> 01:06:50.159
in the Mitzvah of the Rabban

01:06:50.159 --> 01:06:51.159
and we say

01:06:53.159 --> 01:06:54.159
or every Friday night

01:06:54.159 --> 01:06:55.159
before Shabbat

01:06:58.159 --> 01:07:00.159
or every day when we eat bread

01:07:00.159 --> 01:07:01.159
and we say

01:07:03.159 --> 01:07:05.159
Obeying the rabbis.

01:07:05.159 --> 01:07:06.159
Obeying the Jews.

01:07:06.159 --> 01:07:08.159
Were they

01:07:09.159 --> 01:07:10.159
irrational?

01:07:11.159 --> 01:07:12.159
In Gathusha, no.

01:07:12.159 --> 01:07:13.159
On the contrary.

01:07:13.159 --> 01:07:15.159
The laws have a very perfect rationale.

01:07:15.159 --> 01:07:17.159
You understand the context.

01:07:17.159 --> 01:07:19.159
You understand the crisis.

01:07:19.159 --> 01:07:21.159
You understand the circumstances.

01:07:22.159 --> 01:07:23.159
Like for instance

01:07:23.159 --> 01:07:25.159
why there is all of a sudden question about

01:07:26.159 --> 01:07:27.159
who has to bring Mikurim,

01:07:28.159 --> 01:07:29.159
the primitivas,

01:07:29.159 --> 01:07:30.159
the first fruits.

01:07:31.159 --> 01:07:33.159
Things that seem to us esoteric.

01:07:35.159 --> 01:07:37.159
Man dies, leaves his korban,

01:07:37.159 --> 01:07:39.159
his children, do I have to bring it to the Vitamin Gash?

01:07:40.159 --> 01:07:42.159
They were responding to the needs of the hour.

01:07:44.159 --> 01:07:46.159
Things like interest.

01:07:46.159 --> 01:07:47.159
Ah, they...

01:07:47.159 --> 01:07:49.159
No, they know what they're doing.

01:07:49.159 --> 01:07:50.159
There is a rationale.

01:07:50.159 --> 01:07:51.159
You have to study.

01:07:51.159 --> 01:07:52.159
Ask the proper authorities.

01:07:52.159 --> 01:07:53.159
They will teach you.

01:07:54.159 --> 01:07:55.159
Shofar.

01:07:55.159 --> 01:07:56.159
They will teach you.

01:07:57.159 --> 01:07:58.159
And last but not least.

01:07:59.159 --> 01:08:00.159
The system itself.

01:08:03.159 --> 01:08:04.159
Torah.

01:08:04.159 --> 01:08:05.159
Mishnah.

01:08:06.159 --> 01:08:07.159
Gemara.

01:08:08.159 --> 01:08:09.159
Rishonim.

01:08:10.159 --> 01:08:11.159
Shohan Aruch.

01:08:11.159 --> 01:08:12.159
Come and tell us.

01:08:12.159 --> 01:08:13.159
And then you say,

01:08:13.159 --> 01:08:14.159
alright, I don't do this.

01:08:14.159 --> 01:08:15.159
I don't do this.

01:08:17.160 --> 01:08:18.160
Why do you do this?

01:08:18.160 --> 01:08:20.160
Because this is a system of law.

01:08:21.160 --> 01:08:22.160
And a system of law

01:08:22.160 --> 01:08:24.160
needs to be studied.

01:08:24.160 --> 01:08:25.160
To be scrutinized.

01:08:25.160 --> 01:08:27.160
So, I had a lot of fun teaching you this.

01:08:27.160 --> 01:08:28.160
I enjoyed it.

01:08:28.160 --> 01:08:30.160
So I hope you did also.

01:08:30.160 --> 01:08:31.160
And if you have any questions,

01:08:31.160 --> 01:08:32.160
I would like to answer.

01:08:32.160 --> 01:08:34.160
Thank you very much for your attention.

01:08:38.160 --> 01:08:39.160
Yes.

01:08:40.160 --> 01:08:41.160
Alright.

01:08:44.160 --> 01:08:45.160
Oh, thank you.

01:08:45.160 --> 01:08:46.160
Thank you very much.

01:08:59.160 --> 01:09:02.160
Now, I would try to answer.

01:09:02.160 --> 01:09:06.160
But you have to specify the question.

01:09:06.160 --> 01:09:08.160
So, you're talking about the Aruch for Kareem and Shabbat?

01:09:08.160 --> 01:09:09.160
Alright.

01:09:10.160 --> 01:09:11.160
Now.

01:09:14.160 --> 01:09:15.160
First of all.

01:09:16.160 --> 01:09:18.160
Officially, I don't know the answer.

01:09:18.160 --> 01:09:20.160
Why I don't know the answer?

01:09:20.160 --> 01:09:24.160
Because the answer is not explicit.

01:09:27.160 --> 01:09:29.160
But if you study carefully.

01:09:31.160 --> 01:09:32.160
The sources.

01:09:33.160 --> 01:09:35.160
You come to the following situation.

01:09:37.160 --> 01:09:38.160
In order to make Aruch,

01:09:38.160 --> 01:09:41.160
many things are possible to do.

01:09:42.160 --> 01:09:44.160
But you need a few conditions.

01:09:45.160 --> 01:09:46.160
One condition is

01:09:46.160 --> 01:09:50.160
that the inhabitants are all Yehudim.

01:09:52.160 --> 01:09:54.160
If somebody is not Yehudi,

01:09:54.160 --> 01:09:56.160
then you have to buy from him.

01:09:56.160 --> 01:09:57.160
You have to do this.

01:09:57.160 --> 01:09:58.160
You have to do that.

01:09:58.160 --> 01:09:59.160
You have to do this.

01:10:01.160 --> 01:10:04.160
I cannot know for sure that my answer is correct.

01:10:04.160 --> 01:10:06.160
Because that's really what the Hakamim had in mind.

01:10:08.160 --> 01:10:09.160
But I see the benefit of it.

01:10:11.160 --> 01:10:12.160
The benefit of it is

01:10:15.160 --> 01:10:18.160
that we should live among Yehudim.

01:10:19.160 --> 01:10:21.160
And the Aruch is coming very simple.

01:10:22.160 --> 01:10:28.160
If you are in a non-Yehudi or mixed Yehudi, non-Yehudi area,

01:10:28.160 --> 01:10:30.160
you're going to have a tough time making Aruch.

01:10:31.160 --> 01:10:35.160
Is that the real reason why the Hakamim wanted to move?

01:10:35.160 --> 01:10:36.160
No.

01:10:37.160 --> 01:10:39.160
But if that is the reason,

01:10:39.160 --> 01:10:43.160
it makes a lot of sociological sense.

01:10:44.160 --> 01:10:46.160
And you may ponder and think about that.

01:10:46.160 --> 01:10:47.160
Alright?

01:10:48.160 --> 01:10:49.160
Alright.

01:10:49.160 --> 01:10:50.160
Any other...

01:10:52.160 --> 01:10:53.160
No more questions?

01:10:53.160 --> 01:10:54.160
Alright?

01:11:00.160 --> 01:11:01.160
Alright.

